      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lake Hallie is a village in Chippewa County located along the Chippewa River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://gochippewacounty.com/community/lake-hallie/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village derives its name from a nearby oxbow lake situated between Eau Claire and Chippewa Falls.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Hallie%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1843, the McCann brothers and Jeremiah C. Thomas built the Blue Mill, using the lake as a holding pond for logs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Hallie%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Blue Mill later became known as Badger Mills before operations ceased in the 1890s due to a log shortage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Hallie%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Tom Sippel Field serves as the home for the Hallie Eagles, a team in the Chippewa River Baseball League.",
